{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926187Z","id":"18ebef6706263695ad5069b14dd60b00aa19585079da964f4e4fb38a91fe1d1d","body":{"detail":"The shell colours each peer's arrow and name tag by pick_color (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs:239), whose preferred colour is a hash of the person's ID, and memberOf (web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts) makes new people with fresh IDs on every run; two fast renders showed Mia in teal, then in red. The deterministic mode's byte-identical frames (plan Task 2, realtime_determinism) need the people's IDs, or the colours, fixed per run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"ad9592accb8c5f3f34104706d7908901cc250c6e38657b1bdf872837a2b6e550"},"suggested_fix":"Find the source when realtime_determinism first fails: seed the people with fixed IDs if the daemon allows it, or make the colour a function of something the vignette fixes.","summary":"Mia's and Sam's live colours differ from run to run: a deterministic render of realtime will not be byte-identical as it stands","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:24.589423Z","id":"dce532c4f50587cd5116377c007a8b052bee8f8d82e6321c32f0f8a4911be965","body":{"detail":"pick_color (crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs:239-255) gives a person their preferred colour (a hash of their public ID) only when nobody in the room holds it, else the next free one: fixed IDs alone still give other colours if people join in another order, or if someone who holds a colour (the owner's setup page) is still in the room. The daemon mints public IDs at random (new_public_id, crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs) and no API takes one, so the reel fixes the colours without a daemon change: memberIn (web/reel/people.ts) mints invites until the person's public ID hashes (FNV-1a, as live_layers.rs fnv1a) to the colour asked for, revoking the others (DELETE /api/people/invites/{id} frees the name); realtime.ts setup moves Alex's setup page off the artifact before the invites, has Mia (colour 2, teal) and then Sam (colour 0, blue) join before the camera, and fails unless each one's live socket is welcomed in that colour. //web/reel:realtime_determinism: two recordings, 210 frames each, identical.","kind":"comment","references":"18ebef6706263695ad5069b14dd60b00aa19585079da964f4e4fb38a91fe1d1d","summary":"The colour also depends on join order, and the reel now fixes both: people minted to a colour, joining before the camera","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131873Z","id":"4182b67dd13ed8e662848f8535ef69f55cac9dd5d6953c4e37390db4d363b9dc","body":{"detail":"Alex is the hosted daemon's first person, made by the setup page (ownerOf), not by an invite, so memberIn (web/reel/people.ts) cannot mint him to a colour. He joins after Mia and Sam, so he never takes theirs, and the camera films his own view, which draws no pointer or tag for him. A vignette that films someone else's view of the owner, or shows the owner's colour anywhere, has to fix it another way (for example a member as the owner's stand-in, or a daemon-side seed).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":140},"content_hash":"1b8eea9030df5f9494cb44a50c7f27bbfc83eaa4f68834f416fc27d0ce47025c"},"summary":"Alex's own live colour is whatever is free when he joins, a different one each run; nothing on his own screen shows it in this vignette","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/realtime.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:36.797785Z","id":"ccfb5b0a1867af2d1cadfccdb1a84f8d0b6c3637e3afb3bd9c3a3cee103d8115","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3056efdc8764889eda4d9caef5c6a66f0ea071b","summary":"Fixed by a3056efdc: Mia and Sam are minted to live colours 2 and 0 (web/reel/people.ts memberIn) and join before the camera, which checks each welcome colour; bazelisk test //web/reel:realtime_determinism PASSED: 'realtime: two deterministic recordings, 210 frames each, identical'","supersedes":"18ebef6706263695ad5069b14dd60b00aa19585079da964f4e4fb38a91fe1d1d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/history.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:31:19.060594Z","id":"9baf54ec674ed01bdb07bffb59f07f448aff9e3e6ccb5b250378115a692f23fd","body":{"detail":"The daemon has no injectable clock and the camera's page clock stands at REEL_EPOCH (web/reel/camera.ts), so real publish times would show as a calendar date in the version menu and change from day to day. stageTimes rewrites each version's created_at in the #clax-boot block at readystatechange 'interactive', before the shell's module script runs. A page.route fulfil of the document was tried and fails: the fulfilled document loses its local address space and Chromium refuses its <id>.localhost frame (net::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_LOCAL_NETWORK_ACCESS_CHECKS). If the shell starts reading versions from GET /api/artifacts/<id> or the stream instead of the boot block, the menu will show real dates and play() fails its 'staged times' check.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":71},"content_hash":"8e9adaa00b08880bad4f2d863bef2816e1aca87a3fda434c2ac1c0a1af2ba2ff"},"summary":"The history vignette rewrites the camera's shell boot data so versions show staged publish times","tags":["revisit:a test-only daemon clock or created_at override for seeded versions","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/vignettes/history.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T17:31:19.111951Z","id":"c3a81738193ebc41c9e0b168879f2349a5c7910ed52d2299a266703af3c0a935","body":{"detail":"Each version choice is a full shell load (ArtifactController.chooseVersion, location.assign). Without another document holding the clax-stream SharedWorker (web/shell/src/stream.ts:92), each load starts the worker mid film, and the deterministic camera's quiet() waits forever on its script request (it never sees requestfinished for it): 'a frame waited 10 s on .../_clax/shell/stream-worker-*.js'. Any vignette that navigates the camera's shell while filming needs the same keeper, or the camera should leave worker script requests out of its pending set.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"64b82ed591523ba068ddf8be80f6cfe75c508fd5627402a6ca6e7f91abecc34f"},"summary":"A never-filmed gallery tab keeps the shell's SharedWorker alive across the history vignette's navigations","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
